-- title:
--   Per-node conclusion at one end of the descended model
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a non-zero natural number $M'$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a finite set $W$ of places, over the residue field $\kappa(A)$, of the subfield $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa(A),M')$ of $\kappa(A)$-Laurent series generated by the $q$-expansions of $j$ and of $j$ at level $M'$; a containment `hle` of the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the full level-$M'$ modular function field inside the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the $X_H$ function field at level $q^2M'$, $H$ being the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$; a constant reduction $R_0$ over $A$ from the former field to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa(A),M')$, that is, a valuation subring of the source whose residue map to the target is surjective with kernel its maximal ideal and is compatible with $A$, together with a degree-preserving map on places and the two divisor/evaluation laws; a place $s\in W$; an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ with $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$; a natural number $\ell$ and elements $\zeta_0,\varpi_t,\xi\in k_0$; an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with a valuation subring $A_b$ cut out by $A$ and an element $\varpi_b\in A_b$; a prime $\ell'$; an intermediate field $K_\ell$ of $k_0((t))/k_0$ which is an algebra over $A_0:=A\cap k_0$ compatibly with $k_0$; a non-zero $j_\ell\in K_\ell$; $\varpi_t'\in A_0$; an ideal $y$ of the $A_0$-subalgebra of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$; an $A_0$-subalgebra $B_t\subseteq K_\ell$ contained in a valuation subring $W_t$ of $K_\ell$; naturals $n,m$, an element $\gamma_0\in\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, an automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K_\ell$ over $k_0$, an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion of $A_0$ at its maximal ideal, the hypothesis that the level-$q\ell'$ $q$-expansion of $j$ lies in $K_\ell$, an element $a_0\in A_0$, and a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K_\ell$. Assume the bundled frame hypotheses `RigidDescentHyps` for these data. Let $G\le\mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K_\ell)$ be generated by those $\tau$ for which some $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ satisfies `IsLevelAutAt` for $\gamma^{-1}$ at level $(q\ell')^2M'$ with group the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell'$: for every ratio $x=f/g$ of weight-$k$ forms with integral $q$-expansions and every embedding $k_0\to\mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell')}$, the image of $\tau x$ equals the ratio of the $q$-expansions of $f$ and $g$ slashed by the matrix $\begin{pmatrix}a&b/(q\ell')\\(q\ell')c&d\end{pmatrix}$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$. Let $K_0$ be the fixed field of $G$, let $B_0$ consist of the $G$-invariant elements of $B_t$, and let $W_0'$ be the valuation subring of $K_0$ of elements lying in $W_t$. Finally let `nodes` be a finite set of subrings of $K_0$, $\tilde{\mathcal O}$ a subring of $K_\ell$ and $\mathcal O$ a subring of $K_0$ for which the bundled per-end hypotheses `PernodeHyps` hold. Then the predicate `PernodeConclusion` holds for the same data, with $\tilde{\mathcal O}$ dropped from the argument list.
--
--   This is the per-end step in the construction of the descended semistable model of the modular curve at rigid level: from the frame hypotheses `RigidDescentHyps` together with the derived per-end data `PernodeHyps` it produces the per-node block `PernodeConclusion` for one end $\tilde{\mathcal O}$ and the associated subring $\mathcal O$ of the descended field $K_0=K_\ell^G$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.pernodeConclusion_traces_of_rigidDescentHyps`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.pernodeConclusion_traces_of_rigidDescentHyps).
